feat(coupon): the coupon domain joins — templates, user-held instances, the claim caps, and the quote math

Two services in one drop: CouponTemplateService (6 RPCs — the
discount type FIXED_AMOUNT/PERCENTAGE, the validity window, the
redemption caps, the claimable kill-switch, the points price) and
UserCouponService (8 RPCs — the instances plus the Claim and Quote
faces). The golden DDL grows the two tables.

Claim enforces the caps before the instance lands UNUSED: the
claimable flag and the ACTIVE status gate, the template-wide
redemption counter (which ticks on the successful claim), and the
per-user cap over the holder's live rows. The claimant's identity
rides the forwarded x-user-id metadata — the same stamp the cart
write face reads.

Quote walks the discount math: the applicability verdict (UNUSED +
ACTIVE + inside the validity window) and the FIXED_AMOUNT face
value; the PERCENTAGE branch joins the caller's pre-discount total
with the storefront cart phase.

verified over the live stack: the admin template lands (CNY 1000 off,
cap 100/2), the claim mints the UNUSED instance for user 1, and the
quote answers applicable=true with the 1000 face discount
